{"id": "EUVD-2026-103967", "enisaUuid": "4b4a5556-5a6b-3b7f-a4a6-62ba734296dc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: Apply the fine-grained UNDEFs without FEAT_FGT\n\nFGUs don't actually require hardware support, so don't gate fgt trap\nconfig insertion on FGT. This is the only action required to allow FGUs\nalways, as kvm_calculate_traps() already computes the FGU bits with or\nwithout FEAT_FGT.\n\nThis also fixes a spurious WARN when a TLBI OS is run on a guest in vEL1\nwithout FEAT_TLBIOS on non FEAT_FGT hardware. In this configuration the\ncourse-grained HCR_EL2.TTLBOS trap reaches the handler handle_tlbi_el1(),\nwhich expects an EL1 TLBI only from vEL2. With FGUs enabled the UNDEF\nwill be injected without needing the specific handler.\n\n[oliver: Take Wei-Lin's suggested changelog]", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:24:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f4a15c52a552c5244ec27f4ca8bda855594f918", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1113374a17d7f7d16b02ee0bbd9b1e7a60cbb087", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af3300b3a6bace925a496f3520e171c07b999c72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4bdd2b3a708c1feb701cb8b62feb8ad2fd77bb07"], "aliases": ["GHSA-854r-xw42-gj8x", "CVE-2026-98713"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10953f12-dbe8-3eb2-a7ca-08ffbc539e6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "22863298-52ab-3a33-8797-47517987e17b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5a5a406b4b8bb6c1fc7a1e92a872bd86061a53f <2f4a15c52a552c5244ec27f4ca8bda855594f918"}, {"id": "2a249f84-d5d0-389d-bf0c-57852e03263e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5a5a406b4b8bb6c1fc7a1e92a872bd86061a53f <4bdd2b3a708c1feb701cb8b62feb8ad2fd77bb07"}, {"id": "31239f1f-c81f-37ec-818c-0f82a955bfa5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "4aa7487f-624b-39cb-8f7d-6cb025510e1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "556ad529-aade-36ce-8ed8-29c55fc0ebfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9060894b-e4ef-358f-97ac-5dccbd9b7c9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5a5a406b4b8bb6c1fc7a1e92a872bd86061a53f <1113374a17d7f7d16b02ee0bbd9b1e7a60cbb087"}, {"id": "9fce62e8-f238-3b32-af28-8a20b8243b1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e6c24ab2-dde9-3b0b-b54e-bc9adf2bd36e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "eeff4796-4472-313a-bd57-dc620225ff1e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5a5a406b4b8bb6c1fc7a1e92a872bd86061a53f <af3300b3a6bace925a496f3520e171c07b999c72"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "55163495-c564-381f-a0f6-0838dfa2aa14", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}